      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s lending library, the Union City Public Library, has been serving residents since the early 1900s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Union City’s historic district includes the William Kerr House, Raphael Kirshbaum Building, and the Union City Passenger Depot, all on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_City%2C_Indiana",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Platted in 1849, Union City was founded eleven years after its twin city of Union City, Ohio.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
